{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:56d54e303273b2385d3449783a21f349d2db0a7f89e1a2a309c14fcb58b59291","title":"How reliably can observations identify cosmic strings and determine their properties when loop formation sizes are poorly known? The paper treats the macroscopic network-to-observation problem, with particular emphasis on gravitational radiation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56a1f40d01c2f0f9fd6a550b0be7fe9318b52593cb7a27a0de4042b0c02ca94a","title":"How do generalized NS-NS fluxes enter four-dimensional N=1 type-II orientifold theories, and which fluxes charge R-R axions and generate D-term scalar potentials? The motivation is a richer potential for moduli stabilization and possible de Sitter or inflationary applications.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0003"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:561d44bf1dcd69232dc147a807feadab63eca75f135786044f0face2a09deb66","title":"Can left-invariant type IIA coset reductions be justified as consistent truncations, and can their four-dimensional N=2 structure constrain supersymmetric, nonsupersymmetric and de Sitter vacua, including perturbative string-loop effects?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56db8f87d65703ff80f4a3e6811087d0dc9946cfca00e0a456b0f0b0de6a0aee","title":"Can a higher-derivative scalar EFT support stable, isotropic NEC violation with luminal fluctuations and positive scattering amplitudes, and can such a theory admit a local Lorentz-invariant ultraviolet completion?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:566bab49279fecec97511945784f722b340083e352ab4abb2d198fdccce98d3a","title":"Do independently adjustable geometric parameters in supersymmetric massive-IIA AdS₄×S²(B₄) vacua permit scale separation after flux quantisation, and what can curvature ratios and a test-scalar KK spectrum establish?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56189257c4e585b47d5b7b90277e23697dea4b0031668fc46a007d4d3cbeca9d","title":"What are the scalar potential, fermion couplings and superpotentials of the SU(3)-invariant sector of dyonic SO(8) maximal supergravity, and what do they imply for nonsupersymmetric AdS stability and BPS domain walls?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0015"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56bf260292382ba6b171f22d6ecaf87bc0bedbf827e9924624927b89464aec8d","title":"The paper asks whether collective axion mechanisms evade single-axion restrictions on large-field inflation. It seeks consistency tests useful when stabilization and corrections make explicit string constructions difficult to assess.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56708e4c87382e05b4a80581b22ed7619b28fe95e4a6e5e8fbbae6350cc00b70","title":"Can metric Born–Infeld gravity in n≥4 dimensions retain a unique viable maximally symmetric vacuum and only a unitary massless spin-2 excitation while including higher curvature terms?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0020"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56b6532a05622dbc365757681b28f69725ef196b4e805067ec68b6d7951b1403","title":"Can an extension of the Weak Gravity Conjecture to exotic D-brane instantons select admissible instanton-generated superpotentials and constrain their particle-physics consequences?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56e8f846f7e73936b36f128