ions? The scalar space consists of fixed-volume Kähler deformations of a Calabi-Yau threefold, and weak coupling is detected by the full gauge kinetic matrix.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:564bd310d79479177cd5a3ed626f0d7c841610484bf93ee32102db20419cc120","title":"Does a large complex-structure axion displacement universally move its partner saxion in flux compactifications, and which asymptotic powers and flux-dependent delays are possible?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:562e05924736d09cd0a3c357b727302f012b77e47ed8e663104df1ad4974f455","title":"Which consistency conditions follow for single-field k-essence obtained from healthy heavy scalars around Lorentz-breaking backgrounds, and can these permit negative P_XX?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:563984a9c0ee0fd2493ef443164d66a42c7cd93aca2d0c9c7ec5c8d51797a0e5","title":"Can Euclidean black holes and Horowitz–Polchinski (HP) self-gravitating strings connect continuously as classical string backgrounds, and can their thermodynamics generate charged string configurations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56a7c0dfad40620565ed86bfd1495a1d847290e130e8867a8b787a139f64d27d","title":"Does the first quantum correction to the size of the 1+1-dimensional φ⁴ kink support interpreting it as a bound state and provide evidence consistent with the proposed positive lower bound on bound-state radius?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56017bdcddd38ed7cba4066f0d2855ab32f64ec5330fc5104299358b29497dba","title":"Which theoretical advances enable searches for dark matter and early-universe physics, improve cosmological inference, and connect observations to fundamental theory? What work should receive priority over the following decade?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:568f98bb350c08e4e0588f4ed362deedbc587c58874c1d422241f333f0043c57","title":"How can the string one-loop Einstein–Hilbert correction be expressed for Calabi–Yau orientifolds, and how large is its contribution to the Einstein-frame Kähler metric near small-cycle limits?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0080"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:56905029ca360f416938391aca6e294e339db09cdd3bae8fa89383b6ec7409cc","title":"Can membrane nucleation in four-form landscapes select a near-Minkowski vacuum probabilistically, through its longevity, while admitting sufficiently dense vacuum energies and avoiding the empty-universe problem?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0081"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:564f85e2d891497edd3155019661968036fc56e67ac3265e31b3397d10a71a3a","title":"How does stored information resist decay in enhanced-memory systems, how does this mechanism operate in solitons and proposed microscopic black-hole descriptions, and what mass distributions and dark-matter implications might follow for PBHs?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0088"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:565b7ff08372b2e5678b6addd4274268ae7a4773323149e8b064129b9013008c","title":"How do backreaction and large quantum metric fluctuations change neutral and charged emission arbitrarily close to extremality, and what evaporation history follows for an isolated black hole with very large initial charge?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0091"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},